  "description": "Implement core scaled dot-product attention mapping queries, keys, and values to context output vectors.\n\nScaled dot-product attention enables any token to dynamically route information from any other token in O(1) sequential path length.\n\n### Mathematical Formulation\n$$\n\\operatorname{Attention}(Q, K, V) = \\operatorname{softmax}\\left( \\frac{Q K^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}} \\right) V\n$$\n\n### Step-by-Step Implementation\n1. Compute matrix inner products between Query and Key representations\n2. Scale logits by 1/sqrt(d_k) to prevent softmax gradient saturation\n3. Apply softmax across key dimension and project over Value matrix\n\n### Returns\nDictionary with 'output' tensor and normalized attention 'weights'.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Attention Mechanism from Scratch\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\nNatural language consists of discrete words and symbols arranged in sequential order. To process text with neural networks, we convert words into continuous embedding vectors and model their grammatical and semantic relationships. **Attention Mechanism from Scratch** is a core sequence-processing mechanism used in modern Transformer and LLM architectures.\n\nScaled dot-product attention enables any token to dynamically route information from any other token in O(1) sequential path length. In this problem, the goal is to: implement core scaled dot-product attention mapping queries, keys, and values to context output vectors.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe core governing equation for this operation is:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{Attention}(Q, K, V) = \\operatorname{softmax}\\left( \\frac{Q K^T}{\\sqrt{d_k}} \\right) V\n$$\n\nEvery term in this formulation plays a precise mathematical role in ensuring dimensional consistency, numerical stability, and correct algorithmic behavior.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1**: Compute matrix inner products between Query and Key representations\n2. **Phase 2**: Scale logits by 1/sqrt(d_k) to prevent softmax gradient saturation\n3. **Phase 3**: Apply softmax across key dimension and project over Value matrix\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Self-Attention Mechanics**: Scaled dot-product attention computes all-to-all token interactions dynamically, allowing tokens to gather context from the entire sentence simultaneously.\n* **Position Encodings**: Because self-attention is permutation-invariant, positional encodings (like sinusoidal or Rotary Position Embeddings) inject word order into the representations.\n* **Vocabulary & Subwords**: Algorithms like BPE tokenize text into frequent subwords, allowing models to represent rare words without requiring an infinite vocabulary.",
  "examples": [
    "Input: query = [[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]], key = [[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]], value = [[1.0, 2.0], [3.0, 4.0]]\n\nOutput: {\"output\": [[1.6605, 2.6605], [2.3395, 3.3395]], \"weights\": [[0.6698, 0.3302], [0.3302, 0.6698]]}\n\nExplanation: Evaluated pytorch_attention_from_scratch under standard test conditions."
