  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Attention Mechanism from Scratch** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport torch, math, numpy as np\n\ndef pytorch_attention_from_scratch(query: list, key: list, value: list) -> dict:\n    Q, K, V = torch.tensor(query, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(key, dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(value, dtype=torch.float32)\n    w = torch.softmax(torch.matmul(Q, K.transpose(-2, -1)) / math.sqrt(Q.shape[-1]), dim=-1)\n    return {'output': np.round(torch.matmul(w, V).numpy(), 4).tolist(), 'weights': np.round(w.numpy(), 4).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
